    "narrative": "With today\u2019s slate presenting a challenging environment against several elite arms, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** stands as the clear anchor for the Austin Waves, posting a strong 66.77 efficiency score. Despite the threat posed by Peralta, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a favorable 4.32 xERA opposing starter and a significant 14% dynamic platoon boost, making him our highest-projected contributor today. While **Sam Antonacci** and **Brayan Rocchio** are both facing the tougher Williams (2.95 xERA), **Sam Antonacci** retains a higher floor of 47.20 thanks to his prime leadoff spot and a 7% platoon advantage that keeps him in the starting mix despite the high-caliber opposition. \n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved **Liam Hicks**, who finished with a 36.92 score, falling just shy of our 40.00 \"Marginal\" threshold for activation. His matchup against Schlittler is hampered by a pitcher with a sub-3.00 xERA and a negative park factor, which successfully suppressed his upside despite an 11% platoon bump. Meanwhile, **Miguel Vargas** remains in the lineup with a 40.41 score; his inclusion is tenuous given the matchup against Williams and his slightly suppressed xwOBA profile, but he provides more value than **Liam Hicks** today due to the order optimization provided by his spot in the three-hole. With **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** all absent from today's docket due to scheduled off-days, our offensive output will rely heavily on **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** capitalizing on his middle-order opportunities to drive run production in a high-leverage scenario.",
